message.content:
Sure! Below is a simple example of an HTML card that rotates 180 degrees around its Y‑axis when you hover over it. You can copy this into an `.html` file and open it in a browser to see the effect.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Hover‑Rotate Card</title>
<style>
  /* Basic reset */
  * { box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0; padding: 0; }

  body {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    align-items: center;
    height: 100vh;
    background: #f0f0f0;
    font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
  }

  .card-wrapper {
    perspective: 800px;          /* Gives depth to the 3D transform */
  }

  .card {
    width: 300px;
    height: 200px;
    position: relative;
    transform-style: preserve-3d;   /* Needed for 3D children */
    transition: transform 0.6s ease; /* Smooth animation */
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  /* Front side of the card */
  .card .front,
  .card .back {
    position: absolute;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    backface-visibility: hidden;   /* Hide backside when rotated */
    border-radius: 10px;
    overflow: hidden;
    color: white;
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    align-items: center;
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .card .front {
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #ff7e5f, #feb47b);
  }

  .card .back {
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #6a11cb, #2575fc);
    transform: rotateY(180deg);     /* Position back side behind front */
  }

  /* Hover effect – rotate the whole card */
  .card:hover {
    transform: rotateY(180deg);
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="card-wrapper">
  <div class="card">
    <div class="front">
      Front Side
    </div>
    <div class="back">
      Back Side
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

</body>
</html>
```

### How it works

1. **Perspective** – The `.card-wrapper` has `perspective: 800px;`. This gives the 3D space needed for the rotation to look realistic.
2. **Preserve‑3D** – The `.card` uses `transform-style: preserve-3d;` so its child elements keep their 3D positioning.
3. **Backface‑visibility** – Both sides have `backface-visibility: hidden;` so the reverse side disappears when turned away from the viewer.
4. **Rotation** – On hover, the `.card` gets `transform: rotateY(180deg);`, flipping it around the Y‑axis. The back side was initially rotated 180° to sit behind the front.

Feel free to tweak the colors, size, or transition duration to fit your design. Happy coding!
